lyrics_translation_en:
You wish me mad, yet wish me not to live alone;
You want me cold and aloof, yet also flirtatious and base;
You demand I be radiant, yet also alluring without wavering;
You mock my helpless laughter and tears, and mock my heart turned to withered wood;
You grant me dreams, yet grant me swift awakening;
You let me sink into slumber, yet let me waste time without mercy;
You love my purity, yet love me naked, unyielding to decadence;
You watch me sing and play alone, yet watch me break with sorrow;
You wish me ethereal like smoke, yet wish me graceful and languid;
You watch me obsess, yet watch me witty and dignified;
You want me stunningly beautiful, yet want me ruthless without blinking;
You wish me happiness forever, yet wish me wither, never saved;
You charm me, yet leave my eyes dazed;
You seek my genuine affection, yet seek my glances that enchant;
You flee with me secretly, yet demand I serve you as your sole, loyal subject;
You praise my budding beauty, yet praise my obvious, unrestrained desire;
You grant me dreams, yet grant me swift awakening;
You let me sink into slumber, yet let me waste time without mercy;
You love my purity, yet love me naked, unyielding to decadence;
You watch me sing and play alone, yet watch me break with sorrow;
You charm me, yet leave my eyes dazed;
You seek my genuine affection, yet seek my glances that enchant;
You flee with me secretly, yet demand I serve you as your sole, loyal subject;
You praise my budding beauty, yet praise my obvious, unrestrained desire;
You invite me to captivate, yet invite me to exude raw sensuality;
You mirror my full bloom, yet mirror my oxygen-starved, defiant chaos;
You let me be beautiful, yet let me indulge in obsession;
You blame me for carefree serenity at a hundred years old, yet blame me for tears shed in vain.

Cold wind sweeps through, memories freeze solid;
All my efforts echo back with no reply;
Regret stretches on like endless hills;
Pain descends from every direction;
Sorrow invades; vows vanish without a trace;
I can’t find the love we once shared;
You circle overhead like a vulture above loneliness;
Feasting on my longing for you;
Moonlight sways tree shadows, drifting through tropical rainforests;
You never explain why you left;
Your lies were traps—I only realized too late;
Happiness is merely a reflection in water;
Moonlight sways tree shadows, drifting through tropical rainforests;
Sorrow’s rain falls endlessly—my whole body drenched in blood;
That love of mine, sinking deep into swampy mire,
Is heartbreak I’m powerless to stop;
